If the wall is $12.0\ \mathrm{cm}$ thick, with a heat flow surface of $0.08\ \mathrm{m^2}$ and is made of brick of thermal conductivity $0.80\ \mathrm{W\,m^{-1}\,K^{-1}}$,

(i) determine the thermal resistance of the wall;

(ii) hence or otherwise, calculate the rate of heat flow through the wall if $T_1$ is $355\ \mathrm{K}$ and $T_2$ is $330\ \mathrm{K}$.
